## Objective
- Conduct passive reconnaissance and vulnerability assessment of Spare's in-scope web application surface (api.sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, spare.com) for the Spare bug bounty program
- Build a reproducible evidence package with canonical body hashes for report submission

## Important Details
- **Scope IN**: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- **Scope OUT**: ALL other subdomains of sparelabs.com/spare.com; third-party services
- **Rules**: Passive-first (GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps), no account creation, no data modification, sha256 only for secrets
- **Vendor awareness confirmed**: Patch deployed ~2026-08-20 then FULLY REVERTED fleet-wide by ~2026-08-21; multi-version envoy LB serves mixed replica versions; whack-a-mole remediation expected
- **Key architectural insight**: Multi-version envoy LB behind api.sparelabs.com serves two code versions — older vulnerable (prod/CA) and newer patched (staging). Fast replicas (2-17ms) vs slow replicas (500-1500ms) determine bypass behavior. Deterministic routing by source IP.
- **Staging hosts** (api.staging.sparelabs.com, api.staging.us.sparelabs.com): OOS per scope exclusions but confirm prod serves older vulnerable code
- **Fleet hosts confirmed**: prod, us, us2, us3, jp, eu, uat — 8 total (UAT removed from bypass parity post-patch)
- **2026-08-20 patch/revert cycle**: Brief patch window where regions/orgs/auth got 401s; fully reverted; survivor classes (workos/auth, engage chain, org-key) were never in patch batch

