## Objective
- Conduct passive reconnaissance and vulnerability analysis on the Spare bug bounty program surface (spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com)
- Identify, track, and verify unauthenticated security findings across the in-scope API surface for report submission

## Important Details
- **Scope**: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com — ALL OTHER subdomains excluded
- **Rules**: Passive-first (GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps), sha256 for secrets, no account creation, no data modification
- **GitHub repo scan broken**: scan-target misconfigured (gladiaio org instead of sparelabs); 0 files scanned across all sessions — fix clone target before trusting next scan
- **Patch/revert cycle observed**: ~2026-08-20 vendor deployed fix then FULLY REVERTED fleet-wide — findings restored; patch-state conclusions have short half-life; anchor reports to body hashes
- **Multi-version envoy LB**: fast replicas (4ms) vs slow replicas (550-1040ms) serve different code versions; causes flapping between patched/unpatched behavior; deterministic split observed (not probabilistic)
- **longcat triage "PATCHED" (2026-08-11) confirmed FALSE POSITIVE**: only tested no-auth path (400), never tested Bearer-x bypass vector; bypass was 90h+ stable at time of false positive
- **Phase**: RECON on api target
- **Canonical body hashes** used for reproducibility across session resets

